 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of Binghamton\nto establish hotel and motel taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S9432",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9432-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-jj, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9432\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of\nBinghamton to establish hotel and motel taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to authorize the city of Binghamton\nto establish an occupancy tax.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The tax law is amended by adding a new section 1202-jj.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe city of Binghamton Mayor and City Council have requested home rule\nlegislation which would enable them to establish an occupancy tax of up\nto 5% on hotel/motel rooms in the city of Binghamton. The occupancy tax\nis a non-resident tax which, will lessen the burden of real property tax\non residents and will assist the City in meeting its financial obli-\ngations.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications for the State. The\nbill will impose a 5% Occupancy tax on hotel/motel rooms in the City of\nBinghamton.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and sunset in three years.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
